{
  "title": "10: Yunus يونس",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nالٓر تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(1)\nALAAR TILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE HAKEEM.\nA.L.R. These are the ayats of the Book of Wisdom. \nاَكَانَ لِلنَّاسِ عَجَبًا اَنْ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى رَجُلٍ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ اَنْذِرِ النَّاسَ وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَنَّ لَهُمْ قَدَمَ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْؔؕ قَالَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسٰحِرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(2)\nAAKAANA LIN-NAASE A’AJABAN AN AAWHAYNAA ELAA RAJULIN MINHUM AN AANZERE NAASA WA BASH-SHERIL LAZEENA AAMANOO ANNAL LAHUM QADAMA SEDQIN I’NDAL RABBEHEM QAALA KAAFEROON INNAL HAAZAA LASAAHERUN MOBEEN.\nIs it a matter of wonderment to men that We have sent Our inspiration to a man from among themselves? that he should warn mankind (of their danger), and give the good news to the Believers that they have before their Lord the lofty rank of truth. (But) say the Unbelievers: “This is indeed an evident sorcerer!” \nاِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ يُدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَؕ مَا مِنْ شَفِيْعٍ اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اِذْنِهٖ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْهُ ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(3)\nINNAL RABBAKOMUL LAAHO LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL A’RSHIL YUDABBERU AL-AAMRA MAA MIN SHAFEEA’IN ILLAA MIN BA’DE AEZNEH ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM FAAA’BUDOOHU AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nVerily your Lord is Allah, who created the heavens and the earth in six days, and is firmly established on the throne (of authority), regulating and governing all things. No intercessor (can plead with Him) except after His leave (hath been obtained). This is Allah your Lord; Him therefore serve ye: will ye not receive admonition? \nاِلَيْهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقًّا ؕ اِنَّهٗ يَبْدَؤُا الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗ لِيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ بِالْقِسْطِؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَهُمْ شَرَابٌ مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍ وَّعَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(4)\nELAYHE MARJE-O’KUM JAMEE-A’A WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQAN INNAHU YABDA-UL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOHU LE-YAJZEYAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE BIL-QESTE WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAHUM SHARAABUN MIN HAMEEMIN WWAA’AZAABUN ALEEM BEMAA KAANOO YAKFOROON.\nTo Him will be your return- of all of you. The promise of Allah is true and sure. It is He Who beginneth the process of creation, and repeateth it, that He may reward with justice those who believe and work righteousness; but those who reject Him will have draughts of boiling fluids, and a penalty grievous, because they did reject Him. \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ الشَّمْسَ ضِيَآءً وَّالْقَمَرَ نُوْرًا وَّقَدَّرَهٗ مَنَازِلَ لِتَعْلَمُوْا عَدَدَ السِّنِيْنَ وَالْحِسَابَؕ مَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ ذٰلِكَ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّۚ يُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(5)\nHOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA SHAMSA ZEEAAAAN WWAALQAMARA NOORAN WWAQADDARAH MANAAZELA LE-TA’LAMOO A’ADADA AS-SENEENA WAL HESAABA MAA KHALAQAL LAAHO ZAALEKA ILLAA BIL-HAQQE YUFASSELU AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nIt is He Who made the sun to be a shining glory and the moon to be a light (of beauty), and measured out stages for her; that ye might know the number of years and the count (of time). Nowise did Allah create this but in truth and righteousness. (Thus) doth He explain His Signs in detail, for those who understand. \nاِنَّ فِى اخْتِلَافِ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَمَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَّقُوْنَ‏(6)\nINNAL FIL AKHTELAAFE LAYLE WAN NAHAARE WA MAA KHALAQAL LAAHO FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YYATTAQOONA.\nVerily, in the alternation of the night and the day, and in all that Allah hath created, in the heavens and the earth, are signs for those who fear Him. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا وَرَضُوْا بِالْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَاطْمَاَنُّوْا بِهَا وَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَنْ اٰيٰتِنَا غٰفِلُوْنَۙ‏(7)\nINNAL LAZEENA LAA YARJOON LEQAAANAA WARAZOOA BE-HAYAATID DUNYAA WAATMAANNOOA BEHAA WAL LAZEENA HUM A’N AAYAATENAA GHAAFELOON.\nThose who rest not their hope on their meeting with Us, but are pleased and satisfied with the life of the present, and those who heed not Our Signs, \nاُولٰٓئِكَ مَاْوٰٮهُمُ النَّارُ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(8)\nOOLAAA-EKA MAAWAAHUMU TAMASSANAN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nTheir abode is the Fire, because of the (evil) they earned. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ يَهْدِيْهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِاِيْمَانِهِمْۚ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهِمُ الْاَنْهٰرُ فِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِ‏(9)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE YAHDEEHEM RABBOHUM BE-EEMAANEHIM TAJREE MIN TAHTEHEMU ANHAARO FEE JANNATIN NA-E’EM.\nThose who believe, and work righteousness, their Lord will guide them because of their faith: beneath them will flow rivers in gardens of bliss. \nدَعْوٰٮهُمْ فِيْهَا سُبْحٰنَكَ اللّٰهُمَّ وَ تَحِيَّتُهُمْ فِيْهَا سَلٰمٌۚ وَاٰخِرُ دَعْوٰٮهُمْ اَنِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(10)\nDAA’WAAHUM FEEHAA SUBHAANAKA AL-LAAHUMMA WA TAHIYYATOHUM FEEHAA SALAAMUN WAAKHERU DAA’WAAHUM SAALEHAN HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\n(This will be) their cry therein: “Glory to Thee, O Allah!” And “Peace” will be their greeting therein! and the close of their cry will be: “Praise be to Allah, the Cherisher and Sustainer of the worlds!” \nوَلَوْ يُعَجِّلُ اللّٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ الشَّرَّ اسْتِعْجَالَهُمْ بِالْخَيْرِ لَقُضِىَ اِلَيْهِمْ اَجَلُهُمْؕ فَنَذَرُ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(11)\nWA LAW YUA’AJJELU LAAHO LIN-NAASE ASH-SHARRA ASTEA’JAALAHUM BE-KHAYR LAQOZEYA ELAYHIM AAJALUHUM FANAZARU LAZEENA LAA YARJOON LEQAAANAA FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\n If Allah were to hasten for men the ill (they have earned) as they would fain hasten on the good, then would their respite be settled at once. But We leave those who rest not their hope on their meeting with Us, in their trespasses, wandering in distraction to and fro. \nوَاِذَا مَسَّ الْاِنْسَانَ الضُّرُّ دَعَانَا لِجَنْۢبِهٖۤ اَوْ قَاعِدًا اَوْ قَآئِمًا ۚ فَلَمَّا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُ ضُرَّهٗ مَرَّ كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَدْعُنَاۤ اِلٰى ضُرٍّ مَّسَّهٗؕ كَذٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِلْمُسْرِفِيْنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA EZAA MASSAN INSAANA AZ-ZURRU DAA’AANAA LEJANBEH AW QAAE’EDAN AW QAAA-EMAA FALAMMAA KASHAFNAA A’NHO ZURRAH MARRA KA-AN LAM YADU’UNAA ELAA ZURRIN MMASSAH KAZAALEKA ZUYYENA LIL-MUSREFEENA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWhen trouble toucheth a man, He crieth unto Us (in all postures)- lying down on his side, or sitting, or standing. But when We have solved his trouble, he passeth on his way as if he had never cried to Us for a trouble that touched him! thus do the deeds of transgressors seem fair in their eyes! \nوَلَقَدْ اَهْلَكْنَا الْقُرُوْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ لَمَّا ظَلَمُوْا  ۙ وَجَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَمَا كَانُوْا لِيُؤْمِنُوْا  ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْقَوْمَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(13)\nWA LAQAD AHLAKNAL QOROONAL MIN QABLEKUM LAMMAA ZALAMOO WA JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE WA MAA KAANOO LE-YOAMENOO KAZAALEKA NAJZIL QAWMAZ MUJREMEEN.\nGenerations before you We destroyed when they did wrong: their messengers came to them with clear-signs, but they would not believe! thus do We requite those who sin! \nثُمَّ جَعَلْنٰكُمْ خَلٰٓئِفَ فِى الْاَرْضِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ لِنَنْظُرَ كَيْفَ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(14)\nSUMMA JA-A’LNAAKUM KHALAAAEFA FIL ARZE MIN BA’DEHIM LENANZURA KAYFA TA’MALOON.\nThen We made you heirs in the land after them, to see how ye would behave! \nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيَاتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ ۙ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا ائْتِ بِقُرْاٰنٍ غَيْرِ هٰذَاۤ اَوْ بَدِّلْهُ ؕ قُلْ مَا يَكُوْنُ لِىْۤ اَنْ اُبَدِّلَهٗ مِنْ تِلْقَآئِ نَفْسِىْ ۚ اِنْ اَتَّبِعُ اِلَّا مَا يُوْحٰۤى اِلَىَّ ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اِنْ عَصَيْتُ رَبِّىْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(15)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAAYAATUNAA BAYYENAAT QAALA LAZEENA LAA YARJOON LEQAAANAA ATE BEQURAAANIN GHAIRE HAAZAA AW BADDELHU QUL MAA LAHUL LEE AN AUBADDELAH MIN TELQAAE NAFSEE IN AATTABEU’U ILLAA MAA YOOHAA ELAYYA INNEE AKHAAFO IN A’ASAYTU RABBEE A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nBut when Our Clear Signs are rehearsed unto them, those who rest not their hope on their meeting with Us, Say: “Bring us a reading other than this, or change this,” Say: “It is not for me, of my own accord, to change it: I follow naught but what is revealed unto me: if I were to disobey my Lord, I should myself fear the penalty of a Great Day (to come).” \nقُلْ لَّوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَا تَلَوْتُهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكُمْ بِهٖ ۖ  فَقَدْ لَبِثْتُ فِيْكُمْ عُمُرًا مِّنْ قَبْلِهٖ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(16)\nQUL LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA TALAWTUH A’LAYKUM WA LAA AADRAAKUM BEHI FAQAD YAWMAN FEEKUM U’UMURAN MIN QABLEHI AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nSay: “If Allah had so willed, I should not have rehearsed it to you, nor would He have made it known to you. A whole life-time before this have I tarried amongst you: will ye not then understand?” \nفَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ كَذَّبَ بِاٰيٰتِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(17)\nFAMAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW KAZZABA BE-AAYAATEHI INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ MUJREMOON.\nWho doth more wrong than such as forge a lie against Allah, or deny His Signs? But never will prosper those who sin. \nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَضُرُّهُمْ وَلَا يَنْفَعُهُمْ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ شُفَعَآؤُنَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِؕ قُلْ اَتُنَبِّئُوْنَ اللّٰهَ بِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(18)\nWA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YAZURROHUM WA LAA YANFAU’UHUM WA YAQOOLOONA HAAOOLAAA-E SHUFAA’AAUNAA I’NDAL LAAH QUL AATUNABBEOONA LAAHA BEMAA LAA YA’LAMO FIL SAMAAWAATE WA LAA FIL ARZ WALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nThey serve, besides Allah, things that hurt them not nor profit them, and they say: “These are our intercessors with Allah.” Say: “Do ye indeed inform Allah of something He knows not, in the heavens or on earth? Glory to Him! and far is He above the partners they ascribe (to Him)!” \nوَمَا كَانَ النَّاسُ اِلَّاۤ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً فَاخْتَلَفُوْا ؕ وَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ فِيْمَا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(19)\nWA MAA KAANA NAASO ILLAA UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN FA TALAFOO WA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIN RABBEKA LAQOZEYA BAYNAHUM FEEMAA FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nMankind was but one nation, but differed (later). Had it not been for a word that went forth before from thy Lord, their differences would have been settled between them. \nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ ۚ فَقُلْ اِنَّمَا الْغَيْبُ لِلّٰهِ فَانْتَظِرُوْا ۚ اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُنْتَظِرِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA YAQOOLOONA LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE TAA-TEENAA MIN RABBEHI FAQUL INNAMAA AL-GHAYBU LILLAAHE FAANTAZEROOA INNEE MA-A’KUM MENAL AL-MUNTAZEREENA.\nThey say: “Why is not a sign sent down to him from his Lord?” Say: “The Unseen is only for Allah (to know), then wait ye: I too will wait with you.” \nوَاِذَاۤ اَذَقْنَا النَّاسَ رَحْمَةً مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتْهُمْ اِذَا لَهُمْ مَّكْرٌ فِىْۤ اٰيَاتِنَا ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ اَسْرَعُ مَكْرًا ؕ اِنَّ رُسُلَنَا يَكْتُبُوْنَ مَا تَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA EZAA AZAQNAN NAASA RAHMATAM MIN BA’DE ZARAAA-A MASSATHUM EZAA LAHUM MMAKRUN FEE AAAYAATENAA QOLIL LAAHO AASRAU’U MAKRAWN INNAL RUSULANAA YAKTOBOONAL MAA TAMKUROONA.\nWhen We make mankind taste of some mercy after adversity hath touched them, behold! they take to plotting against Our Signs! Say: “Swifter to plan is Allah!” Verily, Our messengers record all the plots that ye make! \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُسَيِّرُكُمْ فِى الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا كُنْتُمْ فِى الْفُلْكِ ۚ وَ جَرَيْنَ بِهِمْ بِرِيْحٍ طَيِّبَةٍ وَّفَرِحُوْا بِهَا جَآءَتْهَا رِيْحٌ عَاصِفٌ وَّجَآءَهُمُ الْمَوْجُ مِنْ كُلِّ مَكَانٍ وَّظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ اُحِيْطَ بِهِمْ ۙ دَعَوُا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَۙ  لَئِنْ اَنْجَيْتَنَا مِنْ هٰذِهٖ لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(22)\nHOWA LAZEE YUSAYRUKUM FIL BARRE WAL BAHRE HATTAA EZAA KUNTUM FIL FULKE WA JARAYNA BEHIM BEREEHIN TAYBATIN WWAFAREHOOA BEHAA JAAATHAA REEHUN A’AASEFUN WWAJAAAHUMU AL-MAWJU MIN KULLE MAKAANIN WWAZANNOOA ANNAHUM AUHEETA BEHIM DA-A’WUL LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUL DEENA LAIL AANJAYTANAA MIN HAAZEHI LANAKOONANNA MENAL ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\nHe it is Who enableth you to traverse through land and sea; so that ye even board ships;- they sail with them with a favourable wind, and they rejoice thereat; then comes a stormy wind and the waves come to them from all sides, and they think they are being overwhelmed: they cry unto Allah, sincerely offering (their) duty unto Him saying, “If thou dost deliver us from this, we shall truly show our gratitude!” \nفَلَمَّاۤ اَنْجٰٮهُمْ اِذَا هُمْ يَبْغُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ ؕ يٰۤاَ يُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنَّمَا بَغْيُكُمْ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِكُمْۙ مَّتَاعَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ثُمَّ اِلَيْنَا مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَنُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(23)\nFALAMMAA AANJAAHUM EZAA HUM YABGHOONA FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE YAA AYYOHAL NAASO INNAMAA BAGHYUKUM A’LAA ANFOSEKUM MMATAAA’A HAYAATID DUNYAA SUMMA ELAYNAA MARJE-O’KUM FANUNABBEUKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nBut when he delivereth them, behold! they transgress insolently through the earth in defiance of right! O mankind! your insolence is against your own souls, an enjoyment of the life of the present: in the end, to Us is your return, and We shall show you the truth of all that ye did. \nاِنَّمَا مَثَلُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا كَمَآءٍ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ فَاخْتَلَطَ بِهٖ نَبَاتُ الْاَرْضِ مِمَّا يَاْكُلُ النَّاسُ وَالْاَنْعَامُؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَخَذَتِ الْاَرْضُ زُخْرُفَهَا وَازَّيَّنَتْ وَظَنَّ اَهْلُهَاۤ اَنَّهُمْ قٰدِرُوْنَ عَلَيْهَاۤ ۙ اَتٰٮهَاۤ اَمْرُنَا لَيْلًا اَوْ نَهَارًا فَجَعَلْنٰهَا حَصِيْدًا كَاَنْ لَّمْ تَغْنَ بِالْاَمْسِ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(24)\nINNAMAA MASALUL HAYAATID DUNYAA KA-MAAA-IM ANZALNAAHO MENAL SAMAAA-E FAAKHTALATA BEHI NABAATU ARZE MIMMAA YAAKULU NAASO WAL AANA’AAMU HATTAA EZAA AAKHAZATE ARZO ZUKHRUFAHAA WAAZZAYNAT WA ZANNAS AAHLUHAA ANNAHUM QAADEROONA A’LAYHAA ATAAHAA AAMRUNAA LAYLAN AW NAHAARAN FA-JA-A’LNAAHAA HASEEDAN KA-AN LAM TAGHNA AMS KAZAALEKA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YATAFAKKAROON.\nThe likeness of the life of the present is as the rain which We send down from the skies: by its mingling arises the produce of the earth- which provides food for men and animals: (It grows) till the earth is clad with its golden ornaments and is decked out (in beauty): the people to whom it belongs think they have all powers of disposal over it: There reaches it Our command by night or by day, and We make it like a harvest clean-mown, as if it had not flourished only the day before! thus do We explain the Signs in detail for those who reflect. \nوَاللّٰهُ يَدْعُوْۤا اِلٰى دَارِ السَّلٰمِؕ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(25)\nWAL LAAHO YAD-O’O ELAA DAARE AS-SALAAME WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nBut Allah doth call to the Home of Peace: He doth guide whom He pleaseth to a way that is straight. \nلِلَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوا الْحُسْنٰى وَزِيَادَةٌ ؕ وَلَا يَرْهَقُ وُجُوْهَهُمْ قَتَرٌ وَّلَا ذِلَّةٌ  ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ ۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(26)\nLILLAZEENA AAHSANOOA AL-HUSNAA WAZEEADATUN WA LAA YARHAQU WUJOOHAHUM QATARUN WA LAA ZELLATUN OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JANNAH HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\n To those who do right is a goodly (reward)- Yea, more (than in measure)! No darkness nor shame shall cover their faces! they are companions of the garden; they will abide therein (for aye)! \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَسَبُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ جَزَآءُ سَيِّئَةٍ ۢ بِمِثْلِهَا ۙ وَتَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌ  ؕ مَا لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ عَاصِمٍ ۚ كَاَنَّمَاۤ اُغْشِيَتْ وُجُوْهُهُمْ قِطَعًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ مُظْلِمًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ ؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(27)\nWAL LAZEENA KASABOOA SAYYE-AATE JAZAAA-O SAYATIN BEMESLEHAA WATARHAQUHUM ZELLATUN MAA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MIN A’AASEMIN KA-ANNAMAA AUGHSHEET WOJOOHOHUM QETAA’AN MENAL LAYLE MUZLEMAN OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nBut those who have earned evil will have a reward of like evil: ignominy will cover their (faces): No defender will they have from (the wrath of) Allah: Their faces will be covered, as it were, with pieces from the depth of the darkness of night: they are companions of the Fire: they will abide therein (for aye)! \nوَيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ نَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا مَكَانَكُمْ اَنْتُمْ وَشُرَكَآؤُكُمْۚ فَزَيَّلْنَا بَيْنَهُمْ وَقَالَ شُرَكَآؤُهُمْ مَّا كُنْتُمْ اِيَّانَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(28)\nWA YAWMA NAHSHURUHUM JAMEE-A’A SUMMA NAQOOLU LILLAZEENA ASHRAKOO MAKAANAKUM ANTUM WASHURAKAAUKUM FAZAYLNAA BAYNAHUM WA QAALA SHURAKAAUHUM MAA KUNTUM IYYAANAA TA’BODOONA.\nOne day shall We gather them all together. Then shall We say to those who joined gods (with Us): “To your place! ye and those ye joined as 'partners' We shall separate them, and their “Partners” shall say: “It was not us that ye worshipped! \nفَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًۢا بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ اِنْ كُنَّا عَنْ عِبَادَتِكُمْ لَغٰفِلِيْنَ‏(29)\nFA KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA BAYNANAA WA BAYNAKUM IN KUNNAA A’N E’EBAADATEKUM LAGHAAFELEENA.\n“Enough is Allah for a witness between us and you: we certainly knew nothing of your worship of us!” \nهُنَالِكَ تَبْلُوْا كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّاۤ اَسْلَفَتْ وَرُدُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَوْلٰٮهُمُ الْحَقِّ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(30)\nHONAALEKAB TABLOOA KULLO NAFSIM MAA AASLAFAT WARUDDOOA ELAL LAAHE MAWLAAHUMU HAQQE WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nThere will every soul prove (the fruits of) the deeds it sent before: they will be brought back to Allah their rightful Lord, and their invented falsehoods will leave them in the lurch. \nقُلْ مَنْ يَّرْزُقُكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اَمَّنْ يَّمْلِكُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَ مَنْ يُّخْرِجُ الْحَىَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَيُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتَ مِنَ الْحَىِّ وَمَنْ يُّدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَؕ فَسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ اللّٰهُۚ فَقُلْ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(31)\nQUL MAN YARZOQOKUM MENAL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE AMMAN FAMANY JA-A’LA LAKOMUS SAM-A’ WA MAN YYUKHREJU HAYYA MENAL MAYYETE WA YUKHREJUL MAYYETA MENAL HAYYE WA MAN YYUDABBERU AL-AAMRA FASAYAQOOLOONA LAAHO FAQUL AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nSay: “Who is it that sustains you (in life) from the sky and from the earth? or who is it that has power over hearing and sight? And who is it that brings out the living from the dead and the dead from the living? and who is it that rules and regulates all affairs?” They will soon say, “Allah”. Say, “will ye not then show piety (to Him)?” \nفَذٰلِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمُ الْحَقُّ  ۚ فَمَاذَا بَعْدَ الْحَقِّ اِلَّا الضَّلٰلُ ۚ فَاَنّٰى تُصْرَفُوْنَ‏(32)\nFAZAALEKUMU LAAHO RABBUKUMU HAQQO FA MAA BA’DA HAQQE ILLAA AZ-ZALAALU FA-ANNAA TUSRAFOONA.\nSuch is Allah, your real Cherisher and Sustainer: apart from truth, what (remains) but error? How then are ye turned away? \nكَذٰلِكَ حَقَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ فَسَقُوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(33)\nKAZAALEKA HAQQAT KALEMATU RABBEKA A’LAL LAZEENA FASAQOOA ANNAHUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThus is the word of thy Lord proved true against those who rebel: Verily they will not believe. \nقُلْ هَلْ مِنْ شُرَكَآئِكُمْ مَّنْ يَّبْدَؤُا الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗ ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ يَبْدَؤُا الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗؕ فَاَنّٰى تُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(34)\nQUL HAL MIN SHURAKAAEKUM MAN YABDAUL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOHU QOLIL LAAHO YABDA-UL KHALQA SUMMA YUE’EEDUH FA-ANNAA TUFAKOONA.\nSay: “Of your 'partners', can any originate creation and repeat it?” Say: “It is Allah Who originates creation and repeats it: then how are ye deluded away (from the truth)?” \nقُلْ هَلْ مِنْ شُرَكَآئِكُمْ مَّنْ يَّهْدِىْۤ اِلَى الْحَقِّؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ يَهْدِىْ لِلْحَقِّؕ اَفَمَنْ يَّهْدِىْۤ اِلَى الْحَقِّ اَحَقُّ اَنْ يُّتَّبَعَ اَمَّنْ لَّا يَهِدِّىْۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّهْدٰىۚ فَمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(35)\nQUL HAL MIN SHURAKAAEKUM MAN YAHDEE ELAL HAQQ QOLIL LAAHO YAHDEE LIL-HAQQE AFAMAWN YAHDEE ELAL HAQQE AHAQQO AN YYUTTABAA’A AMMAN LAA YAHEDDEAA ILLAA AN YYUHDAA FAMAA LAKUM KAYFA TAHKUMOONA.\nSay: “Of your 'partners' is there any that can give any guidance towards truth?” Say: “It is Allah Who gives guidance towards truth, is then He Who gives guidance to truth more worthy to be followed, or he who finds not guidance (himself) unless he is guided? what then is the matter with you? How judge ye?” \nوَمَا يَتَّبِعُ اَكْثَرُهُمْ اِلَّا ظَنًّا ؕاِنَّ الظَّنَّ لَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ شَيْئًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(36)\nWA MAA YATTABEU’U AKSAROHUM ILLAA ZANNAN AENNA AZ-ZANNA LAA YUGHNEE MENAL HAQQE SHAY-ANW INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM BEMAA YAF-A’LOON.\nBut most of them follow nothing but fancy: truly fancy can be of no avail against truth. Verily Allah is well aware of all that they do. \nوَمَا كَانَ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنُ اَنْ يُّفْتَرٰى مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنْ تَصْدِيْقَ الَّذِىْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَتَفْصِيْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ مِنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(37)\nWA MAA KAANA HAAZAA QUR-AANO AN YYUFTARAA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA LAAKIL TASDEEQA LAZEE BAYNA YADAYHE WATAFSEELA KETAABE LAA RAYBA FEEHE MIN RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nThis Qur'an is not such as can be produced by other than Allah; on the contrary it is a confirmation of (revelations) that went before it, and a fuller explanation of the Book - wherein there is no doubt - from the Lord of the worlds. \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ ؕ قُلْ فَاْتُوْا بِسُوْرَةٍ مِّثْلِهٖ وَادْعُوْا مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(38)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU QUL FAATOO BE-SOORATIM MISLEH WAD-O’O MANIS ENIS TA-TA’TUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nOr do they say, “He forged it”? say: “Bring then a Sura like unto it, and call (to your aid) anyone you can besides Allah, if it be ye speak the truth!” \nبَلْ كَذَّبُوْا بِمَا لَمْ يُحِيْطُوْا بِعِلْمِهٖ وَلَمَّا يَاْتِهِمْ تَاْوِيْلُهٗ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ كَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(39)\nBAL KAZZABOO BEMAA LAM YUHEETOOA BE-I’LMEHI WA LAMMAA YAATEHEM TAAWEELUH KAZAALEKA KAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL ZAALEMEEN.\nNay, they charge with falsehood that whose knowledge they cannot compass, even before the elucidation thereof hath reached them: thus did those before them make charges of falsehood: but see what was the end of those who did wrong! \nوَ مِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِهٖ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ لَّا يُؤْمِنُ بِهٖؕ وَرَبُّكَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(40)\nWA MINHUM MAN YOAMENO BEHI WA MINHUM MAN LAA BIL LAAHE BEH WA RABBOKA A-A’LAMO BE-MUFSEDEEN.\nOf them there are some who believe therein, and some who do not: and thy Lord knoweth best those who are out for mischief. \nوَاِنْ كَذَّبُوْكَ فَقُلْ لِّىْ عَمَلِىْ وَلَكُمْ عَمَلُكُمْۚ اَنْتُمْ بَرِيْٓئُوْنَ مِمَّاۤ اَعْمَلُ وَاَنَا بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(41)\nWA KAZZABOOKA FAQUL LEE A’AMALEAA WA LAKUM A’AMALUKUM ANTUM BAREEOONA MIMMAA AAA’MALU ANAT BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TA’MALOON.\nIf they charge thee with falsehood, say: “My work to me, and yours to you! ye are free from responsibility for what I do, and I for what ye do!” \nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّسْتَمِعُوْنَ اِلَيْكَؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تُسْمِعُ الصُّمَّ وَلَوْ كَانُوْا لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(42)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYASTAMEU’OONA AELAYKA AAFAANTA TUSME-U’S SUMMAD WA LAW KAANOO LAA YA’QELOON.\nAmong them are some who (pretend to) listen to thee: But canst thou make the deaf to hear, even though they are without understanding? \nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّنْظُرُ اِلَيْكَ ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تَهْدِى الْعُمْىَ وَ لَوْ كَانُوْا لَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYANZURU ELAYKA AAFAANTA TAHDEAA AL-U’UMAAA WA LAW KAANOO LAA YUBSEROON.\nAnd among them are some who look at thee: but canst thou guide the blind, even though they will not see? \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَظْلِمُ النَّاسَ شَيْئًا وَّلٰكِنَّ النَّاسَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(44)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAZLEMU NAASA SHAY-ANW WA LAAKINNA NAASA ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nVerily Allah will not deal unjustly with man in aught: It is man that wrongs his own soul. \nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَلْبَثُوْۤا اِلَّا سَاعَةً مِّنَ النَّهَارِ يَتَعَارَفُوْنَ بَيْنَهُمْؕ قَدْ خَسِرَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِلِقَآءِ اللّٰهِ وَمَا كَانُوْا مُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(45)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHURUHUM KA-AN LAM YALBASOOA ILLAA SAAA’ATAN MENAL AN-NAHAARE YATAA’AARAFOONA BAYNAHUM QAD KHASERA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BELEQAAE LAAHE WA MAA KAANOO MOHTADEEN.\nOne day He will gather them together: (It will be) as if they had tarried but an hour of a day: they will recognise each other: assuredly those will be lost who denied the meeting with Allah and refused to receive true guidance. \nوَاِمَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ نَعِدُهُمْ اَوْ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَاِلَيْنَا مَرْجِعُهُمْ ثُمَّ اللّٰهُ شَهِيْدٌ عَلٰى مَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(46)\nWA AMMAA NUREENNAKA YAWM LAZEE NAE’EDUHUM AW NATAWAFFAYANNAKA FA ELAYNAA MARJEU’UHUM SUMMA LAAHO WA A’LAA MAA YAF-A’LOON.\nWhether We show thee (realised in thy life-time) some part of what We promise them, or We take thy soul (to Our Mercy) (Before that), in any case, to Us is their return: ultimately Allah is witness, to all that they do. \nوَلِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ رَّسُوْلٌ ۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ رَسُوْلُهُمْ قُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْقِسْطِ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA LEKULLIM UMMATIN RRASOOLUN FA-EZAA JAAA-A RASOOLUHUM QUZEAAA BAYNAHUM BIL QISTE WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nTo every people (was sent) a messenger: when their messenger comes (before them), the matter will be judged between them with justice, and they will not be wronged. \nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(48)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAA WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThey say: “When will this promise come to pass, if ye speak the truth?” \nقُلْ لَّاۤ اَمْلِكُ لِنَفْسِىْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُؕ لِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلٌؕ اِذَا جَآءَ اَجَلُهُمْ فَلَا يَسْتَاخِرُوْنَ سَاعَةً وَّلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُوْنَ‏(49)\nQUL LAA AAMLEKU LE-NAFSEE BEKUM WA LAA BEKUM ILLAA MAA SHAAA-ALLAAH LEKULLIM UMMATIN AAJALUN EZAA JAAA-A AAJALUHUM FALAA YASTAAKHEROONA SAAA’ATAN WA LAA YASTAQDEMOONA.\nSay: “I have no power over any harm or profit to myself except as Allah willeth. To every people is a term appointed: when their term is reached, not an hour can they cause delay, nor (an hour) can they advance (it in anticipation).” \nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ اَتٰٮكُمْ عَذَابُهٗ بَيَاتًا اَوْ نَهَارًا مَّاذَا يَسْتَعْجِلُ مِنْهُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(50)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN AATAAKUM A’AZAABUH BAYAATAN AW NAHAARAN MMAAZAA YASTAA’JELU MINHO MUJREMOON.\nSay: “Do ye see, if His punishment should come to you by night or by day, what portion of it would the sinners wish to hasten? \nاَثُمَّ اِذَا مَا وَقَعَ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِهٖؕ اٰۤلْٴٰنَ وَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(51)\nAASUMMA EZAA MAA WAQA-A’L AAMANTUM BEH AAALAANA WA QAD KUNTUM BEHI TAS-TA’JELOONA.\n“Would ye then believe in it at last, when it actually cometh to pass? (It will then be said): 'Ah! now? and ye wanted (aforetime) to hasten it on!' \nثُمَّ قِيْلَ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْخُلْدِۚ هَلْ تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(52)\nSUMMA QEELA LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL AL-KHULDE HAL TUJZAWNA ILLAA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKSEBOONA.\n“At length will be said to the wrong-doers: 'Taste ye the enduring punishment! ye get but the recompense of what ye earned!'“ \nوَيَسْتَنْۢبِئُوْنَكَ اَحَقٌّ هُوَ ؕؔ قُلْ اِىْ وَرَبِّىْۤ اِنَّهٗ لَحَقٌّ ؔؕ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(53)\nWAYASTANBEOONAKA AAHAQQUN HOWA QUL AEAA WA RABBEE INNAHU LAHAQQUN WA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nThey seek to be informed by thee: “Is that true?” Say: “Aye! by my Lord! it is the very truth! and ye cannot frustrate it!” \nوَلَوْ اَنَّ لِكُلِّ نَفْسٍ ظَلَمَتْ مَا فِى الْاَرْضِ لَافْتَدَتْ بِهٖؕ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّدَامَةَ لَمَّا رَاَوُا الْعَذَابَۚ وَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْقِسْطِ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(54)\nWA LAW ANNAL LEKULLIM NAFSIM ZALAMAT MAA FIL ARZE LAAFTADAT BEH WAASARROOA AN-NADAAMATA LAMMAA RAAWUA A’ZAABA WA BAYNAHUM BIL QISTE WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nEvery soul that hath sinned, if it possessed all that is on earth, would fain give it in ransom: They would declare (their) repentance when they see the penalty: but the judgment between them will be with justice, and no wrong will be done unto them. \nاَلَاۤ اِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(55)\nALAA INNAL LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ ALAA INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nIs it not (the case) that to Allah belongeth whatever is in the heavens and on earth? Is it not (the case) that Allah's promise is assuredly true? Yet most of them understand not. \nهُوَ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(56)\nHOWA YOHYEE WA YOMEETO WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nIt is He Who giveth life and who taketh it, and to Him shall ye all be brought back. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَآءَتْكُمْ مَّوْعِظَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَشِفَآءٌ لِّمَا فِى الصُّدُوْرِۙ  وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(57)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO QAD JAAA-ATKUM MMAWE’EZATUN MIN RABBEKUM WA LEMAA FIL SODOOR WA HODANW WA RAHMATUL LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nO mankind! there hath come to you a direction from your Lord and a healing for the (diseases) in your hearts, and for those who believe, a guidance and a Mercy. \nقُلْ بِفَضْلِ اللّٰهِ وَبِرَحْمَتِهٖ فَبِذٰلِكَ فَلْيَفْرَحُوْا ؕ هُوَ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّا يَجْمَعُوْنَ‏(58)\nQUL BE-FAZLIL LAAHE WA BE-RAHMATEHI FABEZAALEKA FALYAFRAHOOA HOWA KHAYRUL MIMMAA YAJMAU’OONA.\nSay: “In the bounty of Allah. And in His Mercy, in that let them rejoice”: that is better than the (wealth) they hoard. \nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ مِّنْ رِّزْقٍ فَجَعَلْتُمْ مِّنْهُ حَرَامًا وَّحَلٰلًا ؕ قُلْ آٰللّٰهُ اَذِنَ لَكُمْ اَمْ عَلَى اللّٰهِ تَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(59)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM MAA ANZALAL LAAHO LAKUM MIN RREZQIN FAJAA’ALTUM MINHO HARAAMAN WWAHALAALAN QUL AAAALLLAAHU AZENA LAKUM AM A’LAL LAAHE TAFTAROONA.\nSay: “See ye what things Allah hath sent down to you for sustenance? Yet ye hold forbidden some things thereof and (some things) lawful.” Say: “Hath Allah indeed permitted you, or do ye invent (things) to attribute to Allah?” \nوَمَا ظَنُّ الَّذِيْنَ يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(60)\nWA MAA ZANNU LAZEENA YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA YAWMA AL-QEEMATE INNAL LAAHA LAZOO FAZLIN A’LAL NAASE LAAKINNAL AKSARAHUM LAA YASHKOROON.\nAnd what think those who invent lies against Allah, of the Day of Judgment? Verily Allah is full of bounty to mankind, but most of them are ungrateful. \nوَمَا تَكُوْنُ فِىْ شَاْنٍ وَّمَا تَتْلُوْا مِنْهُ مِنْ قُرْاٰنٍ وَّلَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ مِنْ عَمَلٍ اِلَّا كُنَّا عَلَيْكُمْ شُهُوْدًا اِذْ تُفِيْضُوْنَ فِيْهِؕ وَمَا يَعْزُبُ عَنْ رَّبِّكَ مِنْ مِّثْقَالِ ذَرَّةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِى السَّمَآءِ وَلَاۤ اَصْغَرَ مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ وَلَاۤ اَكْبَرَ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(61)\nWA MAA TAKOONO FEE SHAAN WA MAA TATLOO MINHO MIN QURAAANIN WA LAA TA’MALOON MIN A’AMALIN ILLAA KUNNAA A’LAYKUM SHUHOODAN IZ TUFEEZOONA FEEH WA MAA YAA’ZUBU A’N RABBEKA MIN MMESQAALE ZARRATIN FIL ARZE WA LAA FIL SAMAAA-E WA LAA AASGHARA MIN ZAA LEKA WA LAA AAKBARA ILLAA FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nIn whatever business thou mayest be, and whatever portion thou mayest be reciting from the Qur'an, and whatever deed ye (mankind) may be doing, We are witnesses thereof when ye are deeply engrossed therein. Nor is hidden from thy Lord (so much as) the weight of an atom on the earth or in heaven. And not the least and not the greatest of these things but are recorded in a clear record. \nاَلَاۤ اِنَّ اَوْلِيَآءَ اللّٰهِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ ۖ ۚ‏(62)\nALAA INNAL AAWLEEAAAA LAAHE LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nBehold! verily on the friends of Allah there is no fear, nor shall they grieve; \nالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَكَانُوْا يَتَّقُوْنَؕ‏(63)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA KAANOO YATTAQOONA.\nThose who believe and (constantly) guard against evil;- \nلَهُمُ الْبُشْرٰى فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَفِى الْاٰخِرَةِؕ لَا تَبْدِيْلَ لِكَلِمٰتِ اللّٰهِؕ ذٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُؕ‏(64)\nLAHOMUL AL-BUSHRAA FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA AL-AAAKHERATE LAA TABDEELA LEKALEMAATE LAAH ZAALEKA HOWA FAWZUL AL-A’AZEEMU.\nFor them are glad tidings, in the life of the present and in the Hereafter; no change can there be in the words of Allah. This is indeed the supreme felicity. \nوَلَا يَحْزُنْكَ قَوْلُهُمْۘ اِنَّ الْعِزَّةَ لِلّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا ؕ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(65)\nWA LAA YAHZUNKA QAWLOHUM INNAL AL-E’EZZATA LILLAAHE JAMEE-A’A HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nLet not their speech grieve thee: for all power and honour belong to Allah: It is He Who heareth and knoweth (all things). \nاَلَاۤ اِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَمَا يَتَّبِعُ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ شُرَكَآءَ ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَاِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَخْرُصُوْنَ‏(66)\nALAA INNAL LILLAAHE MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAN FIL ARZ WA MAA YATTABEU’U LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE SHORA-KAAA-A IN YYATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA HUM ILLAA YAKHRUSOONA.\nBehold! verily to Allah belong all creatures, in the heavens and on earth. What do they follow who worship as His “partners” other than Allah? They follow nothing but fancy, and they do nothing but lie. \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ لِتَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَالنَّهَارَ مُبْصِرًا ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّسْمَعُوْنَ‏(67)\nHOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA LETASKONOO FEEHE WAN NAHAARA MUBSERAN INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YASMA-O’ON.\nHe it is That hath made you the night that ye may rest therein, and the day to make things visible (to you). Verily in this are signs for those who listen (to His Message). \nقَالُوْا اتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ وَلَدًا سُبْحٰنَهٗ ؕ هُوَ الْغَنِىُّ ؕ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ اِنْ عِنْدَكُمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنٍۢ بِهٰذَا ؕ اَتَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(68)\nQAALOO TAKHAZA LAAHO LAAHO WALADAN HOWA AL-GHANEAAAU LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE IN E’ENDAKUM MIN SULTAANIN BEHAAZAA AATAQOOLOONA A’LAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nThey say: “Allah hath begotten a son!” - Glory be to Him! He is self-sufficient! His are all things in the heavens and on earth! No warrant have ye for this! say ye about Allah what ye know not? \nقُلْ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ لَا يُفْلِحُوْنَؕ‏(69)\nQUL INNAL LAZEENA YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA LAA YUFLEHOONA.\nSay: “Those who invent a lie against Allah will never prosper.” \nمَتَاعٌ فِى الدُّنْيَا ثُمَّ اِلَيْنَا مَرْجِعُهُمْ ثُمَّ نُذِيْقُهُمُ الْعَذَابَ الشَّدِيْدَ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(70)\nLIL-MOTAALLAQAATE FIL DUNYAA SUMMA ELAYNAA MARJEU’UHUM SUMMA NUZEEQUHUMU A’ZAABA ASH-SHADEEDA BEMAA KAANOO YAKFOROON.\nA little enjoyment in this world!- and then, to Us will be their return, then shall We make them taste the severest penalty for their blasphemies. \nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ نُوْحٍۘ اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖ يٰقَوْمِ اِنْ كَانَ كَبُرَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَّقَامِىْ وَتَذْكِيْرِىْ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَعَلَى اللّٰهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ فَاَجْمِعُوْۤا اَمْرَكُمْ وَشُرَكَآءَكُمْ ثُمَّ لَا يَكُنْ اَمْرُكُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ غُمَّةً ثُمَّ اقْضُوْۤا اِلَىَّ وَ لَا تُنْظِرُوْنِ‏(71)\nWAATLU A’LAYHIM NABAANOOHIN IZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI LE-QAWMEHI IN KAANA KABURA A’LAYKUM MMAQAAMEAA WATAZKEEREAA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE FA A’LAL LAAHE TAWAKKALTU FAAJMEU’OOA AAMRAKUM WA SHORAKAAA-AKUM SUMMA LAA YAKUL AAMRUKUM A’LAYKUM GHUMMATAN SUMMA AQZOOA ELAYYA WA LAA TUNZEROONE.\nRelate to them the story of Noah. Behold! he said to his people: “O my people, if it be hard on your (mind) that I should stay (with you) and commemorate the signs of Allah, yet I put my trust in Allah. Get ye then an agreement about your plan and among your partners, so your plan be on to you dark and dubious. Then pass your sentence on me, and give me no respite. \nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَمَا سَاَلْتُكُمْ مِّنْ اَجْرٍؕاِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِۙ وَاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(72)\nFA-IN TAWALLAYTUM FAMAA SAALTUKUM MIN AAJRINAEN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE WA AN A-A’BODA AN SHAY-IWN WA MENAL AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\n“But if ye turn back, (consider): no reward have I asked of you: my reward is only due from Allah, and I have been commanded to be of those who submit to Allah's will (in Islam).” \nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗ فِى الْفُلْكِ وَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ خَلٰٓئِفَ وَاَغْرَقْنَا الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ۚ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(73)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FANAJJAYNAAHU WA MAN MMAA’AH FIL FULKE WA JA-A’LNAAHUM KHALAAAEFA WAAGHRAQNAA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUNZEREEN.\nThey rejected Him, but We delivered him, and those with him, in the Ark, and We made them inherit (the earth), while We overwhelmed in the flood those who rejected Our Signs. Then see what was the end of those who were warned (but heeded not)! \nثُمَّ بَعَثْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ رُسُلًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهِمْ فَجَآءُوْهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَمَا كَانُوْا لِيُؤْمِنُوْا بِمَا كَذَّبُوْا بِهٖ مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَطْبَعُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِ الْمُعْتَدِيْنَ‏(74)\nSUMMA BAA’ASNAA MIN BA’DEHI ROSOLAN ELAA QAWMEHIM FA-JAAA-OOHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAMAA KAANOO LE-YOAMENOO BEMAA KAZZABOO BEHI MIN QABLO KAZAALEKA NATBAU’U A’LAA QOLOOBIL MO’TADEEN.\nThen after him We sent (many) messengers to their peoples: they brought them Clear Signs, but they would not believe what they had already rejected beforehand. Thus do We seal the hearts of the transgressors. \nثُمَّ بَعَثْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ مُّوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَاِ۫ ئِهٖ بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(75)\nSUMMA BAA’ASNAA MIN BA’DEHIM MOOSAA WA AALO ELAA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAA EH BE-AAYAATENAA FAS-TAKBAROO WA KAANOO QAWMAN MMUJREMEENA.\nThen after them sent We Moses and Aaron to Pharaoh and his chiefs with Our Signs. But they were arrogant: they were a people in sin. \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ عِنْدِنَا قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(76)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHOMUL HAQQO MIN I’NDENAA QAALOO INNAL HAAZAA LASEHRUN MOBEEN.\nWhen the Truth did come to them from Us, they said: “This is indeed evident sorcery!” \nقَالَ مُوْسٰٓى اَتَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَكُمْ ؕ اَسِحْرٌ هٰذَا ؕ وَلَا يُفْلِحُ السَّاحِرُوْنَ‏(77)\nQAALA MOOSAA AATAQOOLOONA LIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AKUM AASEHRUN HAAZAA WA LAA YUFLEHUZ AS-SAAHEROONA.\nSaid Moses: “Say ye (this) about the truth when it hath (actually) reached you? Is sorcery (like) this? But sorcerers will not prosper.” \nقَالُوْۤا اَجِئْتَنَا لِتَلْفِتَنَا عَمَّا وَجَدْنَا عَلَيْهِ اٰبَآءَنَا وَتَكُوْنَ لَكُمَا الْكِبْرِيَآءُ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَمَا نَحْنُ لَكُمَا بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(78)\nQAALOO AAJETANAA LETALFETANAA A’MMAA WAJADNAA A’LAYHE AABAAA-ANAA WA TAKOONA LAKOMAA AL-KEBREEAAAU FIL ARZ WA MAA NAHNO LAKOMAA BE-MOAMENEEN.\nThey said: “Hast thou come to us to turn us away from the ways we found our fathers following, in order that thou and thy brother may have greatness in the land? But not we shall believe in you!” \nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ ائْتُوْنِىْ بِكُلِّ سٰحِرٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(79)\nWA QAALA FIRA’WNO ATOONEAA BEKULLE SAAHERIN A’LEEM.\nSaid Pharaoh: “Bring me every sorcerer well versed.” \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ السَّحَرَةُ قَالَ لَهُمْ مُّوْسٰۤى اَلْقُوْا مَاۤ اَنْتُمْ مُّلْقُوْنَ‏(80)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AS-SAHARATU QAALA LAHUM MOOSAA AALQOOA MAA ANTUM MMULQOONA.\nWhen the sorcerers came, Moses said to them: “Throw ye what ye (wish) to throw!” \nفَلَمَّاۤ اَلْقَوْا قَالَ مُوْسٰى مَا جِئْتُمْ بِهِۙ السِّحْرُؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَيُبْطِلُهٗ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُصْلِحُ عَمَلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(81)\nFALAMMAA AALQAWA QAALA MOOSAA MAA JETUM BEHIL AS-SEHRU INNAL LAAHA SAYUBTELUH INNAL LAAHA LAA YUSLEHU A’AMALA MUFSEDEEN.\nWhen they had had their throw, Moses said: “What ye have brought is sorcery: Allah will surely make it of no effect: for Allah prospereth not the work of those who make mischief. \nوَيُحِقُّ اللّٰهُ الْحَقَّ بِكَلِمٰتِهٖ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(82)\nWAYUHEQQU LAAHO HAQQA BEKALEMAATEH WA LAW KAREHA MUJREMOON.\n“And Allah by His words doth prove and establish His truth, however much the sinners may hate it!” \nفَمَاۤ اٰمَنَ لِمُوْسٰٓى اِلَّا ذُرِّيَّةٌ مِّنْ قَوْمِهٖ عَلٰى خَوْفٍ مِّنْ فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ ئِهِمْ اَنْ يَّفْتِنَهُمْ ؕ وَاِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ لَعَالٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ ۚ وَاِنَّهٗ لَمِنَ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(83)\nFAMAA AAMANA LE-MOOSAA ILLAA ZURRIYYATUN MIN QAWMEHI A’LAA KHAWF MIN FIR-A’WNA WAMALAA EHEM AN YYAFTENAHUM WA INNA FIR-A’WNA LAA’AALIN FIL ARZE WA INNAHU LAMENAS MUSREFEEN.\nBut none believed in Moses except some children of his people, because of the fear of Pharaoh and his chiefs, lest they should persecute them; and certainly Pharaoh was mighty on the earth and one who transgressed all bounds. \nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰى يٰقَوْمِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِاللّٰهِ فَعَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلُوْاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمِيْنَ‏(84)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA LE-QAWMEHI IN KUNTUM AAMANTUM BIL-LAAHE FA-A’LAYHE TAWAKKALOOA IN KUNTUM MMUSLEMEENA.\nMoses said: “O my people! If ye do (really) believe in Allah, then in Him put your trust if ye submit (your will to His).” \nفَقَالُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ تَوَكَّلْنَا ۚ رَبَّنَا لَا تَجْعَلْنَا فِتْنَةً لِّلْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(85)\nFA-QAALOO A’LAL LAAHE TAWAKKALNAA RABBANAA LAA TAJA’ALNAA FETNATAN LLELQAWME ZAALEMEEN.\nThey said: “In Allah do we put out trust. Our Lord! make us not a trial for those who practise oppression; \nوَنَجِّنَا بِرَحْمَتِكَ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(86)\nWANAJJENAA BERAHMATEKA MENAL QAWMIL KAAFEREEN.\n“And deliver us by Thy Mercy from those who reject (Thee).” \nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَىٰ مُوْسٰى وَاَخِيْهِ اَنْ تَبَوَّاٰ لِقَوْمِكُمَا بِمِصْرَ بُيُوْتًا وَّاجْعَلُوْا بُيُوْتَكُمْ قِبْلَةً وَّاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(87)\nWA AWHAYNAA AELAA MOOSAA WA AKHEEHE AN TABAWAAA LEQAWMEKUMAA BEMESRA BUYOOTAN WWAAJA’ALOOA BUYOOTAKUM QIBLATAN WA SALAATA WA BASH-SHERIL MOAMENEEN.\nWe inspired Moses and his brother with this Message: “Provide dwellings for your people in Egypt, make your dwellings into places of worship, and establish regular prayers: and give glad tidings to those who believe!” \nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰى رَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّكَ اٰتَيْتَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَاَهٗ زِيْنَةً وَّاَمْوَالًا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۙ رَبَّنَا لِيُضِلُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِكَۚ رَبَّنَا اطْمِسْ عَلٰٓى اَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاشْدُدْ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْا حَتّٰى يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْاَ لِيْمَ‏(88)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA RABBANAA INNAKA AATAYTA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAAH ZEENATAN WWAAMWAALAN FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA RABBANAA LEEZELLOOA A’N SABEELEKA RABBANAA ATMES A’LAA AAMWAALEHEM WAASHDUD A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FALAA YOAMENOO HATTAA YARAWUA A’ZAABA AL-AALEEMA.\nMoses prayed: “Our Lord! Thou hast indeed bestowed on Pharaoh and his chiefs splendour and wealth in the life of the present, and so, Our Lord, they mislead (men) from Thy Path. Deface, our Lord, the features of their wealth, and send hardness to their hearts, so they will not believe until they see the grievous penalty.” \nقَالَ قَدْ اُجِيْبَتْ دَّعْوَتُكُمَا فَاسْتَقِيْمَا وَلَا تَتَّبِعٰٓنِّ سَبِيْلَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(89)\nQAALA QAD AUJEEBAT DDAA’WATUKUMAA FAASTAQEEMAA WA LAA TATTABEA’AAANNE SABEELA LAZEENA LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAllah said: “Accepted is your prayer (O Moses and Aaron)! So stand ye straight, and follow not the path of those who know not.” \nوَجَاوَزْنَا بِبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ الْبَحْرَ فَاَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ وَجُنُوْدُهٗ بَغْيًا وَّعَدْوًا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَدْرَكَهُ الْغَرَقُ قَالَ اٰمَنْتُ اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا الَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنَتْ بِهٖ بَنُوْۤا اِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(90)\nWAJAAWAZNAA BE-BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ BAHRA FAATBAA’AHUM FIRA’WNO WA JONOODOHU BAGHYAN WWAA’ADWAN HATTAA EZAA AADRAKAHU AL-GHARAQU QAALA AAMANTO ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA LAZEE AAAMANAT BEHI BANOOA ISRAAA-EELAZ WA ANAA MENAL AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nWe took the Children of Israel across the sea: Pharaoh and his hosts followed them in insolence and spite. At length, when overwhelmed with the flood, he said: “I believe that there is no god except Him Whom the Children of Israel believe in: I am of those who submit (to Allah in Islam).” \nآٰلْئٰنَ وَقَدْ عَصَيْتَ قَبْلُ وَكُنْتَ مِنَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(91)\nAAAALAANA WA QAD A’ASAYTA QABLO WA KUNTA MENAL MUFSEDEEN.\n(It was said to him): “Ah now!- But a little while before, wast thou in rebellion!- and thou didst mischief (and violence)! \nفَالْيَوْمَ نُنَجِّيْكَ بِبَدَنِكَ لِتَكُوْنَ لِمَنْ خَلْفَكَ اٰيَةً  ؕ وَاِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ النَّاسِ عَنْ اٰيٰتِنَا لَغٰفِلُوْنَ‏(92)\nFALYAWMA NUNAJJEEKA BEBADANEKA LETAKOONA LEMAN-Y KHALFAKA AAYATAL WA INNA KASEERAA MENAL NAASE A’N AAYAATENAA LAGHAAFELOONA.\n“This day shall We save thee in the body, that thou mayest be a sign to those who come after thee! but verily, many among mankind are heedless of Our Signs!” \nوَلَقَدْ بَوَّاْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ مُبَوَّاَ صِدْقٍ وَّرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِۚ فَمَا اخْتَلَفُوْا حَتّٰى جَآءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقْضِىْ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(93)\nWA LAQAD BAWANAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ MUBAWAASEDQIN WWARAZAQNAAHUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE FAMAA TALAFOO HATTAA JAAA-AHOMUL AL-E’ELMU INNAL RABBAKA YAQZEE BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nWe settled the Children of Israel in a beautiful dwelling-place, and provided for them sustenance of the best: it was after knowledge had been granted to them, that they fell into schisms. Verily Allah will judge between them as to the schisms amongst them, on the Day of Judgment. \nفَاِنْ كُنْتَ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ فَسْئَلِ الَّذِيْنَ يَقْرَءُوْنَ الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَۚ لَقَدْ جَآءَكَ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِيْنَۙ‏(94)\nFA-IN KUNTA FEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA ANZALNAA ELAYKA FASALE LAZEENA YAQRAOONA KETAABA MIN QABLEKA LAQAD JAAA-AKA HAQQO MIN RABBEKA FALAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUMTAREEN.\nIf thou wert in doubt as to what We have revealed unto thee, then ask those who have been reading the Book from before thee: the Truth hath indeed come to thee from thy Lord: so be in no wise of those in doubt. \nوَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(95)\nWA LAA TAKOONANNA MENAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE FA TAKOONA MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nNor be of those who reject the signs of Allah, or thou shalt be of those who perish. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ حَقَّتْ عَلَيْهِمْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(96)\nINNAL LAZEENA HAQQAT A’LAYHIM KALEMATU RABBEKA LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThose against whom the word of thy Lord hath been verified would not believe- \nوَلَوْ جَآءَتْهُمْ كُلُّ اٰيَةٍ حَتّٰى يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْاَ لِيْمَ‏(97)\nWA LAW JAAA-AHUM KULLO AAYATIM HATTAA YARAWUA A’ZAABA AL-AALEEMA.\nEven if every Sign was brought unto them, until they see (for themselves) the penalty grievous. \nفَلَوْلَا كَانَتْ قَرْيَةٌ اٰمَنَتْ فَنَفَعَهَاۤ اِيْمَانُهَاۤ اِلَّا قَوْمَ يُوْنُسَ ۚؕ لَمَّاۤ اٰمَنُوْا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُمْ عَذَابَ الْخِزْىِ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَمَتَّعْنٰهُمْ اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(98)\nFA-LAWLAA KAANAT QARYATUN AAAMANAT FANAFAA’AHAA AEEMAANUHAA ILLAA QAWMA YOONUSA LAMMAA AAMANOO KASHAFNAA A’NHUM A’ZAABAL KHIZYE FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WAMATTAA’NAAHUM ELAA HEEN.\nWhy was there not a single township (among those We warned), which believed, so its faith should have profited it, except the people of Jonah? When they believed, We removed from them the penalty of ignominy in the life of the present, and permitted them to enjoy (their life) for a while. \nوَلَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ لَاٰمَنَ مَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ كُلُّهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تُكْرِهُ النَّاسَ حَتّٰى يَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(99)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL RABBOKA LAAMANA MAN FIL ARZE KULLUHUM JAMEE-A’A AAFAANTA TUKREHU NAASA HATTAA YAKOONOOA MUMENEENA.\nIf it had been thy Lord's will, they would all have believed, all who are on earth! wilt thou then compel mankind, against their will, to believe! \nوَمَا كَانَ لِنَفْسٍ اَنْ تُؤْمِنَ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَيَجْعَلُ الرِّجْسَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(100)\nWA MAA KAANA LE-NAFSIM AN TUMENA ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH WAYAJA’ALU A’NKOMUR A’LAL LAZEENA LAA YA’QELOON.\nNo soul can believe, except by the will of Allah, and He will place doubt (or obscurity) on those who will not understand. \nقُلِ انْظُرُوْا مَاذَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ؕ وَمَا تُغْنِى الْاٰيٰتُ وَالنُّذُرُ عَنْ قَوْمٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(101)\nQOLIL ANZUROOA MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA TUGHNEAA AAYAATO WAALNNUZURU A’N QAWMIN LAA YOAMENOONA.\nSay: “Behold all that is in the heavens and on earth”; but neither Signs nor Warners profit those who believe not. \nفَهَلْ يَنْتَظِرُوْنَ اِلَّا مِثْلَ اَيَّامِ الَّذِيْنَ خَلَوْا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ قُلْ فَانْتَظِرُوْۤا اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُنْتَظِرِيْنَ‏(102)\nFA HAL YANTAZEROONA ILLAA MISLA AAYAME LAZEENA KHALAW MIN QABLEHIM QUL FAANTAZEROOA INNEE MA-A’KUM MENAL AL-MUNTAZEREENA.\nDo they then expect (any thing) but (what happened in) the days of the men who passed away before them? Say: “Wait ye then: for I, too, will wait with you.” \nثُمَّ نُنَجِّىْ رُسُلَنَا وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كَذٰلِكَۚ حَقًّا عَلَيْنَا نُنْجِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(103)\nSUMMA NUNAJJEAA RUSULANAA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KAZAALEKA HAQQAN A’LAYNAA NUNJE MOAMENEEN.\nIn the end We deliver Our messengers and those who believe: Thus is it fitting on Our part that We should deliver those who believe! \nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْ دِيْنِىْ فَلَاۤ اَعْبُدُ الَّذِيْنَ تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنْ اَعْبُدُ اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ ۖۚ وَاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(104)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL NAASO IN KUNTUM FEE SHAKKIM MIN DEENEAA FALAA A-A’BODUL LAZEENA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA LAAKIL A-A’BODUL LAAHA LAZEE YATAWAFFAAKUM WA AN A-A’BODA AN SHAY-IWN WA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nSay: “O ye men! If ye are in doubt as to my religion, (behold!) I worship not what ye worship, other than Allah! But I worship Allah - Who will take your souls (at death): I am commanded to be (in the ranks) of the Believers, \nوَاَنْ اَقِمْ وَجْهَكَ لِلدِّيْنِ حَنِيْفًا ۚ وَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(105)\nWA AAQEM WAJHAKA LID-DEENIL HANEEFAA WA LAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\n“And further (thus): 'set thy face towards religion with true piety, and never in any wise be of the Unbelievers; \nوَلَا تَدْعُ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُكَ وَ لَا يَضُرُّكَۚ فَاِنْ فَعَلْتَ فَاِنَّكَ اِذًا مِّنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(106)\nWA LAA TAD-O’ MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFAU’UKA WA LAA YAZURRUKA FA-IN FAA’ALTA FA-INNAKA EZAL MENAL ZAALEMEEN.\n“'Nor call on any, other than Allah;- Such will neither profit thee nor hurt thee: if thou dost, behold! thou shalt certainly be of those who do wrong.'“ \nوَاِنْ يَّمْسَسْكَ اللّٰهُ بِضُرٍّ فَلَا كَاشِفَ لَهٗۤ اِلَّا هُوَ ۚ وَاِنْ يُّرِدْكَ بِخَيْرٍ فَلَا رَآدَّ لِفَضْلِهٖ ؕ يُصِيْبُ بِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ ؕ وَهُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(107)\nWA YYAMSASKA LAAHO BEZURRIN FALAA KAASHEFA LAHU ILLAA HOWA WA YYUREDKA BE-KHAYRIN FALAA RAADDA LE-FAZLEHI YUSEEBU BEHI MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI WA HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nIf Allah do touch thee with hurt, there is none can remove it but He: if He do design some benefit for thee, there is none can keep back His favour: He causeth it to reach whomsoever of His servants He pleaseth. And He is the Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful. \nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَآءَكُمُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْۚ فَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَاِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِىْ لِنَفْسِهٖۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَاِنَّمَا يَضِلُّ عَلَيْهَاۚ وَمَاۤ اَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ بِوَكِيْلٍؕ‏(108)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL NAASO QAD JAAAKUMU HAQQO MIN RABBEKUM FAMANE’ TADAA FA-INNAMAA YAHTADEE LENAFSEHI WA MAN ZALLA FA-INNAMAA YAZELLU A’LAYHAA WA MAA ANAA A’LAYKUM BEWAKEELIN.\nSay: “O ye men! Now Truth hath reached you from your Lord! those who receive guidance, do so for the good of their own souls; those who stray, do so to their own loss: and I am not (set) over you to arrange your affairs.” \nوَاتَّبِعْ مَا يُوْحٰۤى اِلَيْكَ وَاصْبِرْ حَتّٰى يَحْكُمَ اللّٰهُ ۖۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(109)\nWAATTABEA’ MAA YOOHAA ELAYKA WAS BIR HATTAA YAHKUMA LAAHO WA HOWA KHAYRUR HAAKEMEEN.\nFollow thou the inspiration sent unto thee, and be patient and constant, till Allah do decide: for He is the best to decide.",
  "merits": "This Surah is ‘Makki’ and it has 109 verses. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that if a person recites this Surah once in two or three months, he will not be placed alongside the ignorant ones and will be from among the ‘muqarrabeen’ (close ones) on the Day of Reckoning. It is also narrated that if a person recites Surah Yunus, he will get the reward equal to the number of people who were present in the community of Prophet Yunus (a.s.).\nThis Surah can be used as a means of identifying thieves from among your workers. This is done by either writing the Surah and under it writing the names of all the people in the house or workplace who could be suspected of stealing and then keeping this writing in the house. It will, after some time, become manifest who the thief is."
}
